problem.math:
\text{Given a training dataset }\mathcal S \triangleq \bigcup_{i=1}^{n} \{(x_i,y_i)\}\text{ drawn i.i.d. from distribution }\mathcal{D},\text{ we seek to learn a model that generalizes well.}

\text{In particular, consider a family of models parameterized by }w \in \mathcal{W} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^{d};

\text{given a per-data-point loss function }\ell : \mathcal{W} \times \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Y} \to \mathbb{R}_{+},

\text{we define the training set loss }L_{\mathcal S}(w) \triangleq \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n} \ell(w,x_i,y_i)

\text{and the population loss }L_{\mathcal{D}}(w) \triangleq \mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}[\ell(w,x,y)].

